# The night watch (crows_nest: the main deck after dark; Fenn only makes two ratlines). Optional; no puzzle, just the two of them and three stars.
dialogue watch
  node root quill "Two ratlines. Most cargo doesn't leave the deck. Sit. The sky's the same from down here. Just further off."
    > "Two is a personal best. I'd like it entered." -> laugh
      add aff 1
    > "I wanted to see what you see." -> stars
      add aff 1
  node laugh narrator "She laughs, then looks annoyed with both of us."
    -> stars
  node stars quill "Three stars. The Hook, the Lantern, and the Liar. Pell called it that because it moves. Learn those and you'll never be lost."
    > "Which one's the Liar?" -> liar
    > "What do you see, when you look out?" -> see
  node liar quill "That one. No. That one. …See? Liar."
    -> steady
  node steady quill "And when the bow's right, say “steady”, not “straight on”. A wheel likes being told what to keep."
    > "What do you see, when you look out?" -> see
  node see quill "Everywhere I haven't been yet. …What do you see?"
    > "Ink. Every ship I stamped. I wondered where they went." -> ink
      add aff 1
    > "Mostly the mast. It's very close." -> mast
  node ink quill "Well. Now you're one of them."
    -> father
  node mast quill "It does that."
    -> father
  # Fenn says it first. Quill only answers what he tells her.
  node father narrator "The Liar's still up. I start talking about my father. She doesn't stop me."
    > "He left me the compass. Not a dying man's act." -> we
      add aff 1
    > "He owes me three birthdays. I intend to collect." -> collect
      add aff 1
    > "He named the stars wrong on purpose. I'd correct him." -> corrected
      add aff 1
    > "And yours?" if not seen:watch.yours -> yours
  node yours quill "Pell taught me every star up here. He wasn't my father. He just did the useful bits."
    -> yours2
  node yours2 quill "…Third hammock along. Nobody sleeps in it. Go on. Your turn, cargo."
    -> father2
  node father2 narrator "She's quiet. So I keep talking."
    > "He left me the compass. Not a dying man's act." -> we
      add aff 1
    > "He owes me three birthdays. I intend to collect." -> collect
      add aff 1
    > "He named the stars wrong on purpose. I'd correct him." -> corrected
      add aff 1
  node corrected quill "Then he's out there, getting them wrong. Somebody had better go and correct him."
    -> we
  node collect quill "With interest. You're a clerk. You'll have worked it out to the penny."
    -> we
  node we quill "Then we'll find out. …We. Don't read into it."
    > "I'm a clerk. I only read what's written." -> written
      set night_watch
    > "(Say nothing. Watch the Liar.)" -> quiet
      set night_watch
      add aff 1
  node written quill "Then don't write it down either. …Go to bed, cargo. The Liar will still be here. Roughly."
  node quiet narrator "We watch the Liar a long time. It moves, as advertised. Neither of us says she stopped calling me cargo an hour ago."
  node after quill "Still here? The stars don't need supervising, cargo. Well. Not by you."
    > "Show me the Hook again." -> hook
    > "Goodnight, Quill." -> night
  node hook quill "There. A question mark somebody forgot to finish. You'd hate it."
    > "Goodnight, Quill." -> night
  node night quill "Night, cargo. Mind the second ratline."
